{
  "headline": "Norwegian Princess Märtha Louise Marries Self-Styled Shaman in Unconventional Ceremony",
  "body": "The wedding of Princess Märtha Louise of Norway to Durek Verrett, a California-based spiritual healer who identifies as a sixth-generation shaman, took place on Saturday in the scenic but overcast village of Geiranger. The event drew crowds hoping to catch a glimpse of the royal bride. The 52-year-old princess, daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja and fourth in line to Norway’s throne, married Verrett, 49, in a Church of Norway ceremony at the Hotel Union, located near the famous Geiranger fjord. Märtha Louise was accompanied by seven bridesmaids, among them her two daughters, Leah and Emma Behn, from her previous marriage to author Ari Behn, who passed away in 2017. The guest list of about 350 included prominent European royals such as Crown Prince Haakon and Crown Princess Mette-Marit of Norway, Sweden’s Crown Princess Victoria and Prince Daniel, and the Netherlands’ Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien. Known for her non-traditional path, the princess has identified as a clairvoyant and previously ran a school focused on spiritual healing and angel communication. In 2022, she announced her withdrawal from official royal duties to better separate her personal ventures — including her relationship and business with Verrett — from the Norwegian royal family. Verrett, who presents himself on social media as a 'servant of God' and 'energy activator,' counts figures like Gwyneth Paltrow, founder of Goop, among his clients and spiritual connections, referring to her as a 'soul sister.'"
}
```

